menu "Speaker Output"

    config KERN_AUDIO
        bool "Enable speaker output (ES8311 codec)"
        default y
        help
            Compile support for driving the ES8311 audio codec and the
            amplifier behind the board's speaker header. It exists so the
            screen reader has somewhere to speak; nothing else in Kern makes
            sound.

            Building it in does not turn it on: audio_init() is only reached
            when the screen reader is enabled at runtime, which is off by
            default, and the amplifier is powered only while something is
            actually playing.

            The Waveshare boards carry the codec but ship the speaker header
            empty. Without a speaker wired to it this is inert.

    config KERN_AUDIO_I2C_ADDR
        hex "ES8311 I2C address"
        default 0x18
        depends on KERN_AUDIO
        help
            7-bit I2C address of the codec, on the same bus the display and
            camera already use. 0x18 is the ES8311 default and is what every
            Waveshare ESP32-P4 board wires.

    config KERN_AUDIO_MCLK_GPIO
        int "I2S MCLK GPIO"
        default 13
        depends on KERN_AUDIO
        help
            Master clock to the codec, run at 256x the sample rate. The
            defaults for this and the three pins below are shared by every
            Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6-Touch-LCD board.

    config KERN_AUDIO_BCLK_GPIO
        int "I2S BCLK GPIO"
        default 12
        depends on KERN_AUDIO

    config KERN_AUDIO_LRCK_GPIO
        int "I2S LRCK GPIO"
        default 10
        depends on KERN_AUDIO

    config KERN_AUDIO_DOUT_GPIO
        int "I2S data-out GPIO"
        default 9
        depends on KERN_AUDIO

    config KERN_AUDIO_PA_GPIO
        int "Amplifier enable GPIO"
        default 53
        depends on KERN_AUDIO
        help
            Drives the NS4150B enable line, active high. Held low except
            while audio is playing, which keeps the speaker quiet and the
            amplifier unpowered the rest of the time.

    config KERN_AUDIO_VOLUME
        int "Playback volume (0-100)"
        default 70
        range 0 100
        depends on KERN_AUDIO
        help
            DAC volume the codec is programmed with at bring-up. A signer
            that announces itself is a signer that can be overheard, so the
            default sits below the amplifier's full output.

endmenu
